# Copy this to deploy/site.env (gitignored -- never commit the copy) and
# fill in the passphrase the published site sits behind.
#
# This is a third password, and all three are separate:
#   SITE_PASSWORD        reading the published site  (this file)
#   DASHBOARD_PASSWORD   the admin tool at /admin    (deploy/dashboard.env)
#   the deploy key       pushing to GitHub           (no password at all)
#
# It lives in a file rather than in a shell variable because a shell
# variable lasts as long as the shell, and export_static_site.py reads
# this on every build -- including the one a nightly timer runs, where
# there is no shell and nobody to remember.
#
# Leave the file absent for an open site. Removing it from a server whose
# site is currently gated will not silently open the site: the build
# refuses and asks for --no-password, because pages served once in the
# clear stay served.
SITE_PASSWORD=
